  "published": "2026-04-17T12:59:07.097Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### Added\n- **CliRun facade** – new beginner-friendly entry point providing static `RunAsync` / `Run*Async` methods for simple process invocation without boilerplate (zero DI setup required)\n- **ProcessConfigurationFactory** – replaced extension methods with a dedicated static factory class for clearer, more discoverable API\n- **Output redirection mode enhancements** – refactored redirection to use boolean model with clearer semantics\n- **ProcessResult helper extensions** – convenience extensions for working with process results\n- **Design Patterns documentation** – comprehensive guide covering `CliRun`, `IProcessInvoker`, and `ExternalProcess` patterns with trade-off analysis\n\n### Changed\n- **Process cancellation improvements** – cleaner cancellation workflow and improved Unix graceful cancellation handling\n- **ExternalProcess refactoring** – improved code readability and consolidation of start logic; re-added support for custom file path resolver injection\n- **ExitConfiguration refactoring** – replaced static instances with new Create extensions and reworked constructors for better API clarity\n- **Factory method consolidation** – `ProcessConfigurationFactoryExtensions` replaced with static factory class `ProcessConfigurationFactory`\n- **Namespace adjustments** – extensions reorganized for better logical grouping (process piping, cancellation, exit configuration)\n- **Global usings cleanup** – removed redundant global usings to improve dependency clarity\n\n### Removed\n- **ConfigurationInvokationExtensions** – removed as part of factory consolidation and DI pattern improvements\n- **.NET Standard 2.0 conditional compilation** – simplified codebase by removing platform-specific guards\n\n### Fixed\n- **Cancellation warning cleanup** – addressed compiler warnings related to cancellation token handling\n- **Code readability improvements** – refactored process helper classes for clarity and maintainability",
